extraction_notes: "Page span: the heading and lore start at the foot of printed 182 and run onto printed 183, which holds the stat block through the first related-skill lines beside an illustration; the rest of the related skills, equipment, money and cybernetics fill printed 184, where the Intel Specter begins. GROUP: the book files the three ISS classes in their own Coalition Police & Law Enforcement section (printed 178; the contents list them as CS ISS O.C.C.s beside the CS O.C.C.s). None of the five groups names police. Filed men-of-arms with men_of_arms true, like the Peacekeeper: an armed, armored officer under a military command structure with Martial Arts and three W.P.s, and the book''s experience tables (printed 224) put the Specter on the same ladder as the CS Technical Officer and Military Specialist. MONEY: 3D4x1000 credits to start, printed outright, so that is stored rather than a month''s pay; the monthly salary of 4,200 credits and the free apartment are in restrictions. The text layer reads the dice as a cipher; 3D4x1000 and 4200 confirmed from a render. BONUSES: initiative at levels 1, 3, 8 and 12. The book prints one level list for all four saves; +1 each vs magic illusion, mind control, possession and horror factor is read as falling at levels 2, 4, 7, 10, 12 and 15, each step cumulative. INVESTIGATION is a special skill printed with its own base (40% +5% per level) and is kept as a special ability. Surveillance Systems is the catalog''s Surveillance row. LITERACY is printed bare and stored as Literacy: Native Language (American). Pilot: Robots & Power Armor: Basic is the Robots & Power Armor row with no bonus. Hand to Hand is Martial Arts, or Assassin if evil, with no price printed, so the Assassin swap is free. The book prints no language line, so none is stored. Streetwise and Find Contraband are both printed +14%, transcribed as printed. ARMOR: old style Dead Boy armor, the CA-1 heavy or CA-2 light of printed 104, offered as a choice. Weapons, grenades, flares, cross, stakes, nightstick and handcuffs map to the same rows as the ISS Peacekeeper; the C-5 pump pistol is not an energy sidearm and is not offered. Four E-clips for each weapon are stored as eight. Vehicles are prose; see BOOK-INGEST-AUDIT.md F3."
